+Show the App's Config
+---------------------
+
+The ``config`` command prints the loaded application's configuration as
+JSON. This is useful for inspecting the configuration an app actually
+loaded, for example when a value doesn't seem to be applied.
+
+.. code-block:: text
+
+    $ flask config
+    {
+      "DEBUG": false,
+      "SECRET_KEY": "***"
+    }
+
+To avoid printing secrets, the values of any key whose name contains
+``SECRET``, ``PASSWORD``, ``TOKEN``, or ``KEY`` are shown as ``"***"``
+instead of their real value.
+
+
